SUMMARY:Songs of Resilience: Benefit Concert for Immigrant Aid & Defense
DESCRIPTION:This World Refugee Day (June 20)\, join acclaimed composer Sheila Silver and a celebrated group of classical musicians for the premiere of Songs of Resilience\, a concert of original songs rooted in the crises shaping this moment – immigration detention\, displacement\, political resistance\, and more. All ticket proceeds will benefit organizations supporting immigrants and families of immigrants detained at Delaney Hall\, an ICE detention center in Newark\, New Jersey. Beneficiaries include First Friends of New Jersey and New York\, Cosecha\, and St. George’s Episcopal Church’s immigrant relief initiatives. \nSongs of Resilience is co-produced by Silver\, renowned operatic soprano Melissa Citro\, and PROTESTRA. The concert will run approximately 80 minutes\, with a reception to follow. \nIf you are unable to attend the concert but would still like to contribute to the crowdfunding campaign for immigrant aid and defense\, please visit: https://donorbox.org/songs-of-resilience \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
